From c68d6cfe2a4ea8e3fa49dd8204da46a1263a927f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: okhsunrog <me@okhsunrog.dev>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:06:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve authenticated TPM session state across RAM
 restoration

After the complete image signature verifies, pass the fresh NULL-primary context through reserved EFI memory. Bind its one-shot consumer to the original NULL name and handoff address in the signed image header; clear abandoned handoffs and leave in-session reset detection unchanged.
---
 drivers/char/tpm/tpm-interface.c    |  1 +
 drivers/char/tpm/tpm.h              |  1 +
 drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-kernel-key.c  | 84 ++++++++++++++++++++++---
 drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-sessions.c    | 96 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/firmware/efi/efi.c          |  3 +
 drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/tpm.c  | 22 +++++++
 drivers/firmware/efi/tpm-security.c | 34 ++++++++++
 include/linux/efi.h                 | 27 ++++++++
 include/linux/tpm.h                 | 34 +++++-----
 include/linux/tpm_command.h         |  5 ++
 kernel/power/hibernate.c            |  3 +
 kernel/power/hibernate_tpm.c        | 86 +++++++++++++++++++++++---
 kernel/power/power.h                |  2 +
 13 files changed, 358 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)

